{
  "has_chain": true,
  "tags": [
    "theology",
    "knowledge",
    "quran_commentary"
  ],
  "content_type": "creedal",
  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "فَإِنَّهُ رَوَى عَنْهُمْ (عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ) مَا حَدَّثَنَا بِهِ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ هَمَّامٍ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا حَمِيدُ بْنُ زِيَادٍ الْكُوفِيُّ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا الْحَسَنُ بْنُ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ سَمَاعَةَ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا أَحْمَدُ بْنُ الْحَسَنِ الْمَيْثَمِيُّ، عَنْ رَجُلٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ (عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلَامُ) أَنَّهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ:",
      "translations": {
        "en": "For indeed, they (peace be upon them) narrated what was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Hammam, who said: Hamid ibn Ziyad al-Kufi narrated to us, who said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Sama'a narrated to us, who said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Maythami narrated to us, from a man among the companions of Abu Abdillah Ja'far ibn Muhammad (peace be upon them both), that he said: I heard him say:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "نَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الْآيَةُ الَّتِي فِي سُورَةِ الْحَدِيدِ: (وَلَا يَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَمَدُ فَقَسَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ وَكَثِيرٌ مِنْهُمْ فَاسِقُونَ) فِي أَهْلِ زَمَانِ الْغَيْبَةِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: (أَنَ اللَّهَ يُحْيِي الْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا قَدْ بَيَّنَا لَكُمُ الْآيَاتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ) وَقَالَ: إِنَّمَا الْأَمَدُ أَمَدُ الْغَيْبَةِ، فَإِنَّهُ أَرَادَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: يَا أُمَّةَ مُحَمَّدٍ، أَوْ يَا مَعْشَرَ الشِّيعَةِ، لَا تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَمَدُ، فَتَأْوِيلُ هَذِهِ الْآيَةِ جَاءَ فِي أَهْلِ زَمَانِ الْغَيْبَةِ وَأَيَّامِهَا دُونَ غَيْرِهِمْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْأَزْمِنَةِ، وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى نَهَى الشِّيعَةَ عَنِ الشَّكِّ فِي حُجَّةِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى، أَوْ أَنْ يَظُنُّوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى يُخْلِي أَرْضَهُ مِنْهَا طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ، كَمَا قَالَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ) فِي كَلَامِهِ لِكُمَيْلِ بْنِ زِيَادٍ: بَلَى اللَّهُ لَا تَخْلُو الْأَرْضُ مِنْ حُجَّةٍ لِلَّهِ إِمَّا ظَاهِرٌ مَعْلُومٌ، أَوْ خَافٍ مَغْمُورٌ، لِئَلَّا تَبْطُلَ حُجَجُ اللَّهِ وَبَيِّنَاتُهُ، وَحَذَّرَهُمْ مِنْ أَنْ يَشُكُّوا أَوْ يَرْتَابُوا فَيَطُولَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَمَدُ فَتَقْسُوا قُلُوبُهُمْ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "This verse from the Surah al-Hadid: '...and that they should not be like those who were given the Book before, but the time became prolonged to them, so their hearts hardened, and many of them are transgressors' was revealed regarding the people of the time of the Occultation. Then He (the Exalted) said: 'Allah gives life to the earth after its death; indeed, We have made the communications clear to you that you may understand.' And He said: 'Indeed, the 'Amd (period of time) is the period of the Occultation,' for He meant: O nation of Muhammad, or O people of the Shia, do not be like those who were given the Book before, so the time became prolonged to them. The interpretation of this verse came regarding the people of the time of the Occultation and its days, unlike other eras. And indeed, Allah (Exalted) forbade the Shia from doubting the Proof of Allah, or thinking that Allah would leave His earth without Him for a blink of an eye, as Amir al-Mu'minin (peace be upon him) said in his speech to Kumayl ibn Ziyad: 'Yes, Allah, the earth does not remain without a Proof of Allah, either apparent and known, or hidden and concealed, lest the proofs of Allah and His clear signs be invalidated.' And he warned them from doubting or hesitating, so the time would become prolonged to them and their hearts would harden."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "ثُمَّ قَالَ (عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ): أَلَا تَسْمَعُ قَوْلَ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى فِي الْآيَةِ التَّالِيَةِ لِهَذِهِ الْآيَةِ: (اعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يُحْيِي الْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا قَدْ بَيَّنَا لَكُمُ الْآيَاتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ) أَيَ يُحْيِيهَا اللَّهُ بِعَدْلِ الْقَائِمِ عِنْدَ ظُهُورِهِ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا بِجُورِ أَئِمَّةِ الضَّلَالِ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Then he (peace be upon him) said: Do you not hear the saying of Allah (Exalted) in the verse following this verse: 'Know that Allah gives life to the earth after its death; indeed, We have made the communications clear to you that you may understand'? Meaning, Allah gives it life with the justice of the Qa'im (the Rising One) upon his appearance, after its death by the injustice of the Imams of Misguidance."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَتَأْوِيلُ كُلِّ آيَةٍ مِنْهَا مُصَدِّقٌ لِلْأُخْرَى وَعَلَى أَنَّ قَوْلَهُمْ (صَلَوَاتُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِمْ) لَا يَبْدُ أَنْ يَصِحَّ فِي شَذْوذٍ مَنْ يَشْذُّ، وَفِتْنَةٍ مَنْ يَفْتَنُ، وَنُكُوصٍ مَنْ يَنْكُصُ عَلَى عَقِبَيْهِ مِنَ الشِّيعَةِ بِالْبَلْبَلَةِ وَالْمُحَيْصِ وَالْغَرْبَلَةِ الَّتِي قَدْ أَوْرَدْنَا مَا ذَكَرُوهُ (عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ) مِنْهُ بِأَسَانِيدَ فِي بَابِ مَا يَلْحَقُ الشِّيعَةَ مِنَ الْمُحَيْصِ وَالتَّفَرُّقِ وَالْفِتْنَةِ، إِلَّا أَنَّا نَذْكُرُ فِي هَذَا الْمَوْضِعِ حَدِيثًا أَوْ حَدِيثَيْنِ مِنْ جُمْلَةِ مَا أَوْرَدْنَا فِي ذَلِكَ الْبَابِ لِئَلَّا يَنْكَرَ مَنْكَرٌ مَا حَدَثَ مِنْ هَذِهِ الْفُرَقِ الْعَامِلَةِ بِالْأَهْوَاءِ الْمُؤَثِّرَةِ لِلدُّنْيَا.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "The interpretation of each of these verses confirms the other, and it is upon the saying of them (peace be upon them) that it must be correct regarding the deviation of whoever deviates, the trial of whoever is tried, and the turning back of whoever turns back on his heels from the Shia with confusion, sifting, and screening, which we have cited with their chains in the chapter of what befalls the Shia of sifting, division, and trial. However, we mention here one or two traditions from what we cited in that chapter, lest a denier deny what has occurred from these sects acting on their fancies, preferring the worldly life."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "وَهُوَ مَا أَخْبَرَنَا بِهِ أَحْمَدُ بْنُ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ سَعِيدِ بْنِ عُقْدَةَ الْكُوفِيُّ، وَهَذَا الرَّجُلُ مِنْ مَنْ لَا يُطْعَنُ عَلَيْهِ فِي الثِّقَةِ وَلَا فِي الْعِلْمِ بِالْحَدِيثِ وَالرِّجَالِ النَّاقِلِينَ لَهُ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا عَلِيُّ بْنُ الْحَسَنِ التَّيْمَلِيُّ مِنْ تَيْمِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنِي أَخَوَايَ أَحْمَدُ وَمُحَمَّدُ ابْنَا الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ فَضَالٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِمَا، عَنْ ثَعْلَبَةَ بْنِ مَيْمُونَ، عَنْ أَبِي كَهْمَسٍ، عَنْ عِمْرَانَ بْنِ مَيْثَمٍ، عَنْ مَالِكِ بْنِ ضَمْرَةَ، قَالَ:",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And it is what Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Uqda al-Kufi informed us of, and this man is one of those who are not faulted in reliability and knowledge of hadith and the narrators who transmit it, who said: Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Taymali from Taym Allah narrated to me, who said: My two brothers Ahmad and Muhammad, sons of al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Fadhal, narrated to me, from their father, from Tha'laba ibn Maymum, from Abu Kahmas, from Imran ibn Maytham, from Malik ibn Dhamra, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ) لِسَاقِيهِ: كُونُوا فِي النَّاسِ كَالنَّحْلِ فِي الطَّيْرِ، لَيْسَ شَيْءٌ مِنَ الطَّيْرِ إِلَّا وَهُوَ يَسْتَضْعِفُهَا، وَلَوْ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِي أَجْوَافِهَا لَمْ يَفْعَلْ بِهَا كَمَا يَفْعَلُ، خَالِطُوا النَّاسَ بِأَبْدَانِكُمْ، وَزَايِلُوهُمْ بِقُلُوبِكُمْ وَأَعْمَالِكُمْ، فَإِنَّ لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مَا اكْتَسَبَ وَهُوَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مَعَ مَنْ أَحَبَّ، أَمَا إِنَّكُمْ لَنْ تَرَوْا مَا تُحِبُّونَ وَمَا تَأْمَلُونَ - يَا مَعْشَرَ الشِّيعَةِ - حَتَّى يَتْفِلَ بَعْضُكُمْ فِي وُجُوهِ بَعْضٍ، وَحَتَّى يُسَمِّيَ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضًا كَذَّابِينَ، وَحَتَّى لَا يَبْقَى مِنْكُمْ عَلَى هَذَا الْأَمْرِ إِلَّا كَالْكُحْلِ فِي الْعَيْنِ، أَوِ كَالْمِلْحِ فِي الطَّعَامِ، وَهُوَ أَقَلُّ الزَّادِ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Amir al-Mu'minin (peace be upon him) said to his Shia: 'Be among the people like bees among birds; no bird is but it considers them weak, and if it knew what was in their interiors, it would not treat them as it does. Mix with people with your bodies, and separate from them with your hearts and deeds, for every person has what he earned, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be with whom he loved. Indeed, you will not see what you love and what you hope for - O people of the Shia - until some of you spit in the faces of others, until some of you call others liars, and until none of you remains upon this matter except like the kohl in the eye, or like the salt in food, which is the least of the sustenance.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَسَأَضْرِبُ لَكُمْ فِي ذَلِكَ مَثَلًا: وَهُوَ كَمَثَلِ رَجُلٍ كَانَ لَهُ طَعَامٌ قَدْ ذَرَاهُ وَغَرَبَلَهُ وَنَقَاهُ وَجَعَلَهُ فِي بَيْتٍ وَأَغْلَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْبَابَ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ فَتَحَ الْبَابَ عَنْهُ فَإِذَا السُّوسُ قَدْ وَقَعَ فِيهِ، ثُمَّ أَخْرَجَهُ وَنَقَاهُ وَذَرَاهُ، ثُمَّ جَعَلَهُ فِي الْبَيْتِ وَأَغْلَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْبَابَ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ فَتَحَ الْبَابَ عَنْهُ فَإِذَا السُّوسُ قَدْ وَقَعَ فِيهِ، وَأَخْرَجَهُ وَنَقَاهُ وَذَرَاهُ، ثُمَّ جَعَلَهُ فِي الْبَيْتِ وَأَغْلَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْبَابَ، ثُمَّ أَخْرَجَهُ بَعْدَ حِينٍ فَوَجَدَهُ قَدْ وَقَعَ فِيهِ السُّوسُ، فَفَعَلَ بِهِ كَمَا فَعَلَ مَرَارًا حَتَّى بَقِيَ مِنْهُ رِزْمَةٌ كَرِزْمَةِ الْأَنْدَرِ الَّذِي لَا يُضِرُّهُ السُّوسُ شَيْئًا، وَكَذَلِكَ أَنْتُمْ تُحَيْصُكُمُ الْفِتَنُ حَتَّى لَا يَبْقَى إِلَّا عِصَابَةٌ لَا تُضِرُّهَا الْفِتَنُ شَيْئًا.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And I will give you an example of this: It is like the example of a man who had food which he winnowed, sifted, and purified, and put it in a house and closed its door for as long as Allah willed. Then he opened the door, and the weevils had fallen into it. Then he took it out, purified it, and winnowed it, and put it back in the house and closed its door for as long as Allah willed. Then he opened the door, and the weevils had fallen into it again. He took it out, purified it, and winnowed it, and put it back in the house and closed its door. Then he took it out after a while and found that the weevils had fallen into it. He did with it as he had done many times until only a bundle remained, like the 'Andar' (a type of grain resistant to weevils) which is not harmed by weevils at all. So too, you will be sifted by trials until only a small group remains, whom the trials will not harm at all."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَرُوِيَ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ (عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ) أَنَّهُ قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ لَتُمَحَّصُنَّ وَاللَّهِ لَتَطَيَّرُنَّ يَمِينًا وَشِمَالًا حَتَّى لَا يَبْقَى مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا كُلُّ امْرِئٍ أَخَذَ اللَّهُ مِيثَاقَهُ وَكَتَبَ الْإِيمَانَ فِي قَلْبِهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِرُوحٍ مِنْهُ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And it is narrated from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) that he said: 'By Allah, you will be purified, and by Allah, you will be scattered right and left, until none of you remains except every person whom Allah took his covenant, and wrote faith in his heart, and strengthened him with a spirit from Him.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَفِي رِوَايَةٍ أُخْرَى، عَنْهُمْ (عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ): حَتَّى لَا يَبْقَى مِنْكُمْ عَلَى هَذَا الْأَمْرِ إِلَّا الْأَنْدَرُ فَالْأَنْدَرُ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And in another narration, from them (peace be upon them): 'Until none of you remains upon this matter except the 'Andar' (the purest/fewest) and the 'Andar'.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَهَذِهِ الْعِصَابَةُ الَّتِي تَبْقَى عَلَى هَذَا الْأَمْرِ وَتَثْبُتُ وَتُقِيمُ عَلَى الْحَقِّ هِيَ الَّتِي أُمِرَتْ بِالصَّبْرِ فِي حَالِ الْغَيْبَةِ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And this small group that remains upon this matter, stands firm, and upholds the truth, is the one that was ordered to be patient during the time of the Occultation."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "فَمِنْ ذَلِكَ، مَا أَخْبَرَنَا بِهِ عَلِيُّ بْنُ أَحْمَدَ الْبَنْدَنِيْجِيُّ، عَنْ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مُوسَى الْعَلَوِيِّ الْعَبَّاسِيِّ، عَنْ هَارُونَ بْنِ مُسْلِمٍ، عَنِ الْقَاسِمِ بْنِ عُرْوَةَ، عَنْ بُرَيْدِ بْنِ مُعَاوِيَةَ الْعَجْلِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ الْبَاقِرِ (عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ) فِي مَعْنَى قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى: (يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اصْبِرُوا وَصَابِرُوا وَرَابِطُوا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ) قَالَ:",
      "translations": {
